    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Figure 3. Base b = 1+2i with all possible one missing digit."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 83,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.672, 344.87, 485.328, 372.92 ],
    "font" : "CMR12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "of Hausdorff the metric. With one missing digit, Cb,D is 1/N1/2(b)close to Cb,D"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 85,
    "level" : "2",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.672, 313.81, 485.329, 357.622 ],
    "font" : "CMR12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : ". Notice that Cb,D is self-similar whose contraction ratio is 1/N1/2(b). From here, we see that the thickness of Cb,D is at least cdN1/2(b) for some constant cd > 0. □"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 84,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 191.257, 343.963, 194.531, 349.94 ],
